n tests; failures map cleanly to a single task.\n- `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench <name> -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` — quick benches that catch P99 regressions on hot paths.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile && npm run lint && npm test` — extension TypeScript compile, lint, and runner.\n- `test -f <path>` + `grep -q '## Heading' <path>` — doc-producing tasks confirm structural completeness.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::<x>` — contract-gate tasks have their own dedicated test module.\n\nThe final readiness review (R89) runs the full `cargo test --workspace`, full extension compile/lint/test, and asserts every prior review file exists and is closed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out-of-scope (per spec audit)\n\nThe spec lists nothing out of scope. This plan plans all of it. The \"First Implementation Slice\" steps in the spec (event log → memory graph → retrieval V1 → consolidation → verification) appear first inside their phases, but every later phase still ships in this build per the execution philosophy.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Files this plan produces (summary)\n\nThe complete file inventory for the build is the union of every `files_expected` array in [`tasks.json`](tasks.json). Major groupings:\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/**` — Phase 1.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/**` — Phase 2.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/**` — Phase 3.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/**` — Phase 4.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/**` — Phase 5.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/**` — Phase 6.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/**` — Phase 7.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/**` — Phase 9.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/**` — Phase 11.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/**` — cross-layer gates.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/**` and `rpc/memory_v2/**` — Phase 8.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture.rs`, `working_memory_tool.rs`, `metrics_surface.rs`, `mcp_schema_tests.rs`, `mcp_compat_tests.rs` — instrumentation + contract tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — CLI regression report.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/**` — baseline + benchmark suites.\n- `extension/src/review/**` — Phase 10 review UI.\n- `extension/src/test/**` — extension UI smoke + contract tests.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-*.md` — design notes per phase.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-*.md` — operator + migration + benchmark + UI guides + runbook + recovery playbook.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R*.md` — all review outputs.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Where the per-task briefs live\n\nEvery task (`Txx`) and every review (`Rxx`) has a markdown file under [`tasks/`](tasks/) with: goal, prerequisites, inputs, steps, files-expected, verification commands, coding-standard checks, and definition-of-done for that task. Executors should open the next pending task's file before touching code.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
