inistic jobs: duplicate detection, supersession candidates, demote unused/low-value memories, mark stale memories after graph changes, refresh memories whose evidence still matches.\n- T42 — LLM-driven jobs: episode summary, procedure extraction from repeated successful workflows, contradiction detection, failure-pattern extraction. MUST run only in background or manual-review modes, never on synchronous post-task hot path.\n- T43 — LLM provenance: each proposal records model, prompt hash, response hash. Queue depth bounded. Cost and latency budgets documented per job type in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md`. Failed/malformed responses leave prior memory unchanged and emit consolidation failure event.\n- T44 — manual review queue for high-scope (repo + organization) memory changes.\n- T45 — replay-safe execution: jobs can be replayed; provenance + prior state preserved.\n- T46 — integration tests: proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events.\n- R47 — Phase 6 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T48 — verification engine core: file/symbol/doc/test existence checks. Outputs from spec §Verification Engine: verified/unverified/in_review/stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated.\n- T49 — exact-span evidence validation: when evidence captured an exact span, validate the span text still matches.\n- T50 — branch/workspace scope enforcement (deny leakage). Negative tests required.\n- T51 — time-bound expiry + incremental verification triggered by graph changes (large repos cannot tolerate full rescans).\n- T52 — stale surfacing in workflow bundles + label discipline: stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as trusted guidance. Non-negotiable from spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n- T53 — integration tests: stale never displayed as trusted; scope leakage blocked.\n- R54 — Phase 7 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R55 — contract gate Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval. Required headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, `## Scope-filter round-trip`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. Adds new test file `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` per tasks.json `files_expected`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json. Coding-standard checks must include the standard limits (file ≤800, function ≤50, nesting ≤3) and no-broken-windows rules.\n\nWrite all 17 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4404,"cache_read_input_tokens":124894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4404},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"26932ac7-0b08-40e1-933a-1affd91de867","request_id":"req_011Cb7MVwhDZjFqnUfLkL1CZ"}
